<k>gallimond</k>
<b><c c="darkmagenta">▪ <c>I.</c></c></b> 	<b><abr>†</abr>  ˈgallimond, <abr>adv.</abr></b> <i><abr>Obs.</abr></i>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><c c="gray">[Of obscure origin; perh. a var. of <kref>gallimand</kref> n., or f. the place-name Gallimont.]</c></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> In a state of disorder; confusedly.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex>[<b><i>c</i> 1275</b> <i>Ancr. Gloss.</i> 14 <c c="darkmagenta">Þe hous stod al galimaund [Ashby MS. galimaund].</c>]</ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><b><i>a</i> 1400</b> <i>Sir Cleges</i> 212 <c c="darkmagenta">Hys men ran gallimond aboute.</c> <b><i>c</i> 1400</b> <i>Rolls of Parlt.</i> III. 44 <c c="darkmagenta">The town lay gallimond.</c> <b>1487</b> <i>T. Marlow</i> <i>Chron.</i> 91 <c c="darkmagenta">All thynges were gallymonde.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">2.</c></b> Hence, at random; without plan.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><b>1502</b> <i>W. Prine</i> <i>Serm.</i> 8 <c c="darkmagenta">To wander gallimond.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<b><c c="darkmagenta">▪ <c>II.</c></c></b> 	<b>ˈgallimond, <abr>n.</abr></b>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote>(<c c="darkslategray">ˈgælɪmɒnd</c>)</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><c c="gray">[f. sense I: see above.]</c></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> A confused heap; a jumble.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">b.</c></b> <i>spec.</i> A dish of mixed scraps.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><b>1611</b> <i>A. Bysshe</i> <i>Housew.</i> 30 <c c="darkmagenta">A gallimond of cold meats.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">2.</c></b> A person of disordered habits.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<b><c c="darkmagenta">▪ <c>III.</c></c></b> 	<b><abr>†</abr>  ˈgallimond, <abr>a.</abr></b> <i><abr>Obs.</abr></i>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><abr>†</abr> <b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> Disordered; confused.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">2.</c></b> Of speech: rambling.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<b><c c="darkmagenta">▪ <c>IV.</c></c></b> 	<b>ˈgallimond, <abr>v.</abr></b>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">I.</c></b> <i>intr.</i> To move confusedly.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> To run about in disorder.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">II.</c></b> <i>trans.</i> To throw into disorder.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">2.</c></b> To jumble (things) together.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">a.</c></b> With <i>up</i>.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<b><c c="darkmagenta">▪ <c>V.</c></c></b> 	<b>ˈgallimond, <abr>n.</abr><sup>2</sup></b>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><b><c c="indigo">1.</c></b> A local name for the corn marigold.</blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
<blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><blockquote><ex><b>1847</b> <i>Bot. Gloss.</i> 55 <c c="darkmagenta">Gallimond, the corn marigold.</c></ex></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote>
